  "id": "COMPOUND:32178 - PROTEIN:83",
  "verbalization": "Cryptobeilic Acid B appears to interact with the Glucagon receptor through multiple indirect pathways, with the Glucagon receptor being a target in at least three distinct biological processes. The first pathway links Cryptobeilic Acid B to Tyrosine--tRNA ligase, which is targeted by (+)-Conocarpan, and the second pathway connects Cryptobeilic Acid B to Taste receptor type 2 member 31, which is targeted by Npc158230. The third pathway involves Cryptobeilic Acid B targeting Taste receptor type 2 member 31 again, but this time through Triptogelin G-2. These findings suggest that Cryptobeilic Acid B may act as a modulator of the Glucagon receptor via different receptor types, possibly through distinct signaling mechanisms. The shared target of the Glucagon receptor across these pathways implies a potential role for Cryptobeilic Acid B in regulating glucose metabolism or other downstream processes involving the Glucagon receptor. The evidence supports a mechanism where Cryptobeilic Acid B influences the Glucagon receptor through receptor-targeted pathways, though the exact molecular mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
